  "body": "Fixes #4336\n\n## What\n\n`eachHourOfInterval` with a fractional step below 1 (e.g. `0.5`) never advances the date: `date.setHours(date.getHours() + step)` silently discards the fraction, so the loop appends the same date forever and hangs. The Temporal implementation instead throws `RangeError` for fractional steps (including `1.5`).\n\n## Fix\n\nTruncate the step toward zero with `Math.trunc` in both implementations before the sign handling and the zero check:\n\n- `pkgs/core/src/eachHourOfInterval/index.ts` (Date)\n- `pkgs/core/src/tp/eachHourOfInterval/index.ts` (Temporal)\n\nThis gives both implementations the same whole-hour behavior:\n- `step: 0.5` / `step: -0.5` → truncated to zero → `[]`\n- `step: 1.5` → behaves like `step: 1`\n- `step: -1.5` → behaves like `step: -1`\n\n## Tests\n\nAdded regression tests in `pkgs/core/src/eachHourOfInterval/test.ts` for positive, negative, and truncate-to-zero fractional steps. Results:\n\n- `pnpm vitest run eachHourOfInterval --project \"main\"`: 24/24 pass\n- `pnpm lint`: clean\n- `pnpm types`: clean",
